{"generated":"2026-10-11T04:39:43.475Z","flood_attached":true,"method":"Buildings: every way or multipolygon relation tagged building=* in the Geofabrik Puerto Rico extract of OpenStreetMap; one record per OSM object, outer ring only. ADDED footprints (buildings_added; buildings = buildings_osm + buildings_added): machine detections from imagery carried by Overture Maps release 2026-09-23.1 (Google Open Buildings, Microsoft ML Buildings), not surveyed, not in OpenStreetMap. OpenStreetMap is the base: every building of our own OSM extract is kept unchanged. An Overture building is added only if none of its sources is OpenStreetMap and (1) it does not overlap our OSM extract or an addition already accepted: dropped if its centroid is inside an OSM footprint, an OSM centroid is inside it, or the outlines intersect at all (outer rings); (2) it is plausible: at least 25 m2, confidence at least 0.7 where the source gives one, not above 5000 m2 unless its confidence is at least 0.8, and at least 4 m wide (short side of its smallest enclosing rectangle; containers, trailers and vehicles are narrower); (3) its centroid is on land inside a municipio; (4) it is not a small footprint (under 60 m2) whose outline comes within 1.5 m of an OSM footprint (taken as part of the mapped building). Tests run in that order and a candidate is counted under the first one it fails. Added records have bit 7 (0x80) of kind set; kind is house under 400 m2, otherwise other; height is the source's own or 0. They count in every number here exactly like OSM buildings; their kind is a guess from area alone. Ground elevation: bilinear sample of the AWS Terrain Tiles Terrarium zoom-14 tile (USGS 3DEP 1/3 arc-second, about 10 m, on land) at the centroid of the outer ring; samples are clamped at the tile edge. It is the ground at one point, not the floor height. Flood class: FEMA National Flood Hazard Layer flood hazard zones (NFHL MapServer layer 28, DFIRM_ID LIKE '72%'), point-in-polygon at the building centroid; highest class wins where polygons overlap. 3 = V/VE, 2 = A/AE/AH/AO/A99/AR, 1 = X with 0.2 PCT subtype, 0 = anything else or no polygon. at_or_below: inclusive counts of buildings with ground elevation <= 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 3 and 5 m (buildings below 0 included). Use these for \"at or below +X m\": the histogram bins are half-open, so summing bins 0..3 gives \"< 1.0 m\" and leaves out the buildings sitting on the exact 1.0 m terrace. buildings_sfha = classes 2 + 3. elev_hist: counts of buildings by ground elevation in 0.25 m bins from 0 to 10 m, bin i = [i*0.25, (i+1)*0.25); below_0 and above_10 hold the rest; elev_unknown where no elevation tile was available. CAVEAT on the elevation source: in the low coastal plains (San Juan metro, Ponce and others) the Terrain Tiles surface has flat terraces at whole metres (most at exactly 3.0, 7.0, 10.0 and 13.0 m), so it is not lidar-grade there and counts near those levels are lumpy; qa.json elevation.integer_plateaus gives the numbers. Treat \"at or below 1 m / 2 m\" as an order of magnitude until a lidar DEM replaces it. \"At or below X m\" from these bins is a bathtub screen: it is not a hydrodynamic model and does not test hydrological connection to the sea. OpenStreetMap completeness varies by municipio; counts are of mapped footprints (plus the added machine detections), not of housing units or parcels. Kinds: 0 house/residential (including building=yes under 400 m2), 1 apartments, 2 commercial, 3 industrial, 4 civic, 5 religious, 6 other (including building=yes of 400 m2 or more).","sources":{"buildings":{"name":"OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL 1.0)","extract":"https://download.geofabrik.de/north-america/us/puerto-rico-latest.osm.pbf","extract_headers":[],"extract_timestamp":"2026-10-09T20:21:04Z"},"buildings_added":{"name":"Overture Maps Foundation, buildings theme: features whose origin is not OpenStreetMap (footprints detected from imagery by machine learning)","release":"2026-09-23.1","url":"s3://overtu